    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "The digest tests pass again after a fix in `tests/fakes.py`. `app/`, the pytest configuration and the pinned packages are unchanged.\n\n**Why the mocks stopped working:** openai 3.19.2 sends its requests through a separate package, `httpx2`, instead of `httpx`. respx only patches `httpx`, so its router never saw the OpenAI requests, and they went to the real network.\n\n**The fix:** `mock_openai()` now also patches `httpx2.HTTPTransport.handle_request` for the duration of the `with` block.\n- The patch is on the class, not on individual clients, so it covers app.digest's cached client and clients created before the block as well as inside it. It's removed when the block exits.\n- `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions` gets the next canned reply, or a 400 once the replies run out. Both the mock and respx record request bodies the same way.\n- Any other httpx2 request inside the block raises an `AssertionError` instead of going to the network. This matches respx's default of rejecting requests it has no route for.\n- The respx router is still there, so clients built on legacy `httpx.Client` (openai 3.x still accepts those) are handled too.\n- The helper's interface is the same: `mock_openai(*replies)` still yields the list of request bodies.\n\n**Checks:** the two digest tests pass. I also ran a throwaway test of the rest of the docstring, and it passed:\n- a client created before the block got the canned reply;\n- a request beyond the canned replies got a 400;\n- a request after the block went to the real network. It was blocked because the test environment has no network access, which is why the run shows one socket warning.\n\n**One thing for you to do:** I couldn't delete that throwaway test because the `rm` needed approval. Please delete `tests/test_zz_check.py`. Once it's gone, the suite is just the two digest tests and the warning goes away.\n\nThe docstring says this helper was copied into the ops-bot repo. If ops-bot is on openai 3.x too, its copy probably needs the"
  },
